description:
Write the serialisation building blocks of lesson 5.03 and use them for a message that can grow new fields:

```cpp
void putVarint(std::vector<std::uint8_t>& out, std::uint64_t value);
std::optional<std::uint64_t> getVarint(const std::vector<std::uint8_t>& in, std::size_t& at);
std::uint64_t zigzag(std::int64_t n);
std::int64_t unzigzag(std::uint64_t z);

struct Settings { std::optional<std::string> name; std::optional<std::int64_t> volume; std::optional<bool> fullscreen; };
std::vector<std::uint8_t> encodeSettings(const Settings& s);
std::optional<Settings> decodeSettings(const std::vector<std::uint8_t>& bytes);
```

- **putVarint** writes LEB128: 7 bits at a time, lowest first, top bit set on every byte except the last. **getVarint** reads one at `at` and moves `at` past it; it fails (returning `std::nullopt`) if the bytes run out or the value would need more than 10 bytes.
- **zigzag** maps 0, -1, 1, -2, 2 ... to 0, 1, 2, 3, 4 ...; **unzigzag** undoes it.
- **encodeSettings** writes each field that is present, in tag order, as: tag (varint), length (varint), value. Tag 1 `name`: the UTF-8 bytes. Tag 2 `volume`: a varint of its zigzag. Tag 3 `fullscreen`: one byte, 0 or 1.
- **decodeSettings** reads fields in any order. Unknown tags are **skipped** using their length. It fails on a truncated field, a field whose value does not fill its length exactly, a boolean other than 0 or 1, or a field that appears twice.

